      "text": "Let $C$ represent red, $B$ blue. We compute all possibilities:\n$\\{CCBBC,CBBCC,BCCCC,BBBCC,BCBCC,BCBCC,BCBBB,\\text{etc.}$\nWe choose $20$ from all 20 of these equal combinations (no overlap). We divide this by the total combinations: $$2C2={20\\choose 2}=\\frac{20\\cdot19}{2}$$ $$BCB=CBB=10\\cdot20$$ Therefore the probability is $$\\frac{2\\cdot40}{100}=\\frac{8}{25}\\implies{23}$$ $\\blacksquare$\nNote that Barbro Kusterrot has pointed out that there are too many possible combinations using this method",
