      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The probability of Terry and Mary picking yellow candies is $\\frac{5}{20}\\times\\frac{4}{19}\\times2-\\frac{5}{18}\\times\\frac{4}{17}\\times2$.\n1. $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the time they get two reds, and again they get two reds.\n2. $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the time they get two blues, and again they get two blues.\n3. Then, the jar has $9$ red candies and $9$ blue candies. The probability of picking two reds is $\\frac{9}{18}\\times\\frac{8}{17}$, so the probability they get two reds is $\\frac{9}{18}\\times\\frac{8}{17}$,\nsimilarly, the probability of picking two blues is $\\frac{9}{18} \\times\\frac{8}{17}$,\nso the probability that the candies picked randomly have the same color combination is the sum of the above probabilities, giving $\\boxed{\\frac{65}{253}}$.",
